# Cloud Yatra browser configuration.
# All values are public client configuration; never place credentials here.
# Leave Faro/dashboard values empty for a fully local run.

# Backend Worker base URL (Cloudflare Worker + D1). When set, the game forwards telemetry
# to it and uses the shared cross-player leaderboard. Leave EMPTY for a fully local,
# offline-safe build (local leaderboard + no telemetry ingest). Public, not a secret.
# Example: https://cloud-yatra-api.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Grafana Faro collector URL from Frontend Observability.
VITE_FARO_URL=
# Usually leave EMPTY. Grafana Cloud Faro receivers embed the app key in the collector URL
# itself (…/collect/<key>), so VITE_FARO_URL alone is enough to send RUM — RUM will still
# arrive with this unset. Only fill this in if your receiver is configured to require a
# separate public app key in addition to the URL.
VITE_FARO_APP_KEY=
# The Grafana PUBLIC dashboard embedded inline below the game. Grafana Cloud sends CSP
# frame-ancestors 'none' on its dashboards, so the Worker reverse-proxies the public
# dashboard under its own origin (/public-dashboards/... + the Grafana SPA paths) with the
# frame-blocking headers stripped, and the game page iframes that proxied URL. Set this to
# the Grafana "Share externally" URL of cloud-yatra-observatory-public.json:
#   https://<your-org>.grafana.net/public-dashboards/<token>
# The game rewrites it to ${VITE_API_BASE_URL}/public-dashboards/<token> for the embed.
VITE_GRAFANA_DASHBOARD_URL=

# OPTIONAL: an authenticated "game-in-dashboard" source URL (/d/<uid>/...), used only as a
# fallback open-in-new-tab link if the inline embed can't load. Example:
#   https://<your-org>.grafana.net/d/cloud-yatra-np/cloud-yatra-observatory
VITE_GRAFANA_GRAND_URL=
